WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.960
Hey Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:06.209
This tower of testosterone is Danish man-beast
Peter Freuchen.

00:00:06.209 --> 00:00:12.420
He’s like a cross between Hodor and James
Bond, “The name’s Hodor, Hodor Hodor”.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:18.260
During his life Peter Freuchen was an arctic
explorer, doctor, anthropologist, zoologist,

00:00:18.260 --> 00:00:23.279
journalist, actor, author, and generally just
a badass adventurer.

00:00:23.279 --> 00:00:27.670
He is the most interesting man in the world
and I hear he drinks Dos Equis.

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:33.480
In 1906, after studying at university to become
a doctor, Freuchen went on his first of several

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.970
arctic expeditions, when he was just 20-years-old.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:42.320
Peter sailed as far north as he could and
then rode a dogsled 2,000 kilometres north,

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:48.250
across Greenland, in the perishing cold, facing
hunger, frostbite, polar bears and wolves.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:52.950
It was during this expedition that he discovered
he enjoyed living like an invincible badass

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:58.580
in the nipple-biting cold so much that he
didn’t return from his trip and instead

00:00:58.580 --> 00:01:03.420
lived with native Inuit people whom he discovered
in Thule, Greenland.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:08.150
He lived with the Inuit people for over two
decades, during this time he married one of

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:12.890
their women, gave her two children, killed
a wolf with his bare hands when it attacked

00:01:12.890 --> 00:01:18.460
him, established a trading base in Thule and
led seven arctic expeditions.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:23.110
Because that’s just what you do when you’re
a 6 foot 7 man-titan called Peter Freuchen

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:26.620
and you wear a huge polar bear coat to match
your incredible man-beard.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:31.850
It’s written that the coat is made from
a polar bear he killed himself, but I think

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:35.960
the bear was so scared of Freuchen that it
sheared itself in front of him and left.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:43.380
One of Peter’s Expeditions involved trekking
1,000 kilometres across Greenland with a friend

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:48.760
just to prove to him that Greenland is not
separated from the North Pole by a river,

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.800
of course he was correct.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:53.060
The two men nearly died during this trip.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:57.860
But Freuchen’s closest call was on a later
expedition in 1926.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:01.370
He got caught in a raging blizzard and took
cover underneath his dogsled.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:06.880
The snow trapped him inside the sled and formed
a large ice cave around him, he had unwittingly

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:08.670
created his own tomb.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:14.710
It was so tight and claustrophobic in there
that his beard froze to the ice beneath him,

00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:20.490
meaning he had to rip his beard off, just
to turn his head, which of course he did.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:25.840
Some say the testosterone contained in Peter’s
lost beard have caused the polar ice caps

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:28.450
to melt, out of fear.

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:31.660
So how did Freuchen escape his icy tomb?

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:38.010
You’re not gonna believe this – he fashioned
a shiv out of his own hardened feces and used

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:41.800
it to dig his way out of several metres of
ice.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:47.350
After escaping Peter discovered he had frostbite
up both his legs and all of his toes had contracted

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.690
gangrene.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:56.220
So he crawled three hours back to base, prised
his frozen socks off then amputated his gangrenous

00:02:56.220 --> 00:03:00.130
toes with a pair of pliers and a hammer.

00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:04.380
He used no anesthesia and he wasn’t even
slightly pissed.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:10.000
Peter never drank alcohol because if he ever
got into a bar fight he could potentially

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:12.459
punch a hole in the ozone layer.

00:03:12.459 --> 00:03:16.959
In the 1930s he returned to Denmark, wrote
for a newspaper for a while and then wrote

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:22.040
not one but thirty books and several scientific
papers.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:26.459
He became a prizewinning, bestselling author,
because that’s just what you do when you’re

00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:28.870
the most interesting man in the world.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:34.959
His first wife died of the Spanish Flu in
1921 but he went on to marry a Danish multi-millionaire’s

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:40.020
daughter; her parents ran a margarine business.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:44.930
They liked Peter so much that they made him
editor-in-chief of a magazine, which is still

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:50.050
in circulation today and is the longest running
Danish magazine in history.

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:55.530
Freuchen also led expeditions to South Africa
and Siberia just for the hell of it, and also

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:59.960
because his prolonged presence in Denmark
and Greenland was causing a shift in the tectonic

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.280
plates.

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:05.110
Freuchen then wrote, directed and starred
in several movies.

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:09.989
The most well-known of which is called “Eskimo”;
it went on to win an Oscar.

00:04:09.989 --> 00:04:14.989
Nazi film director Leni Riefenstahl attended
the film’s premiere, she was actually Hitler’s

00:04:14.989 --> 00:04:16.400
favourite director.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:21.440
According to witnesses Freuchen lifted her
out of her seat and spun her in circles above

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.520
his head whilst laughing his arse off.

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:25.520
Why?

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.699
Because spinning Nazis is what Peter Freuchen
does for fun.

00:04:28.699 --> 00:04:29.930
Speaking of Nazis.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:34.949
Peter Freuchen was Jewish and during the war
he was a major figure in the Danish Resistance

00:04:34.949 --> 00:04:41.009
movement, hiding refugees and he completely
messed up several Nazi operations.

00:04:41.009 --> 00:04:45.830
He angered the Reich so much that they arrested
him and sentenced him to death.

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:51.650
He singlehandedly escaped and fled to Sweden
where he continued to mess up Hitler’s plans

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:53.080
until the end of the war.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:57.309
Come on, this dude shit-daggered his way out
of an ice coffin, he’s wasn’t going to

00:04:57.309 --> 00:05:01.030
let himself be killed by a bunch of Nazis.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:05.830
Aged 60, Freuchen spent his remaining years
in New York where he “claimed”, I mean

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:10.039
married another woman, who was a major player
at Vogue magazine.

00:05:10.039 --> 00:05:14.789
He became best friends with American super
star Mae West and bench pressed Jean Harlow

00:05:14.789 --> 00:05:16.199
at a party once.

00:05:16.199 --> 00:05:22.939
Finally, he became only the fifth person in
history to answer the $64,000 question, winning

00:05:22.939 --> 00:05:26.129
the TV game show “The $64,000 Question”.

00:05:26.129 --> 00:05:31.900
A year later he was awarded the Gold Medal
by the International Benjamin Franklin Society

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:35.479
for his “services to mankind in opening
new frontiers.”

00:05:35.479 --> 00:05:43.139
He then wrote yet another book and died three
days later in 1956, aged 71.

00:05:43.139 --> 00:05:49.379
Some say he never died but was simply hired
to replace God, because he could do a much

00:05:49.379 --> 00:05:59.849
better job.

00:05:59.849 --> 00:06:15.559
Thanks for watching.

